claimed: deploy-paas -- stage 2 (specs/deployment.md): the fly, render
and railway targets.

Three platforms, three shapes: fly is one app per service so it renders
a fly.toml per service, render is a Blueprint and takes the whole
system in one file, railway is per-service JSON. A managed database is
DELEGATED rather than refused where the platform has one (the file
cannot express it, the platform can) -- the exact commands go in a
setup.sh, the same way the cluster target ships secrets.sh.

The gate is a REAL PARSER per format, not a golden file: stage 1 just
demonstrated that a golden test passes happily on output the consuming
tool rejects. tomllib for fly.toml, ruby -ryaml for render.yaml, okay's
own Json for railway.json -- the shelling ones Live, per AGENTS.md.

Needs a small model addition: Need.Region, which stage 3 wants too.

Files: okay-deploy Paas.scala + Deployment.scala (Need.Region) +
Targets.scala, tests, okay-script's rendered targets, specs, boards.
